          "targetDoi": "10.1016/j.injury.2024.111401",
          "snippet": "4 The modified anterior tension band (MATB) technique is a reliable technique for open reduction and internal fixation of patellar fractures, and this surgical technique is relatively mature.  9  However, the direction of stress in longitudinal patellar fractures differs from that of transverse fractures, with lower tension and mainly shear forces parallel to the fracture line, making the MATB fixation, which is centered on converting tension into pressure, no longer applicable. In addition, the postoperative pain due to metal stimulation also affects the therapeutic efficacy of the MATB technique in treating patellar fractures.",
