          "targetDoi": "10.1016/j.injury.2024.111401",
          "snippet": "In the MATB technique, patients are prone to develop postoperative pain and other reactions related to metal foreign bodies,  9  ,  10  while the fixation technique described in this article reduces irritation and improves the repair effect of longitudinal patellar fractures. In addition, this technique is performed completely under arthroscopy, which is less traumatic for the patient.",
          "section": "discussion",
          "type": "mentioning"
