      ],
      "isOa": true,
      "fulltextExcerpts": [
        "Among them, transverse fractures are the most common, and the incidence of longitudinal fractures is relatively low. For this reason, most current surgical treatments are developed for transverse or comminuted fractures,7,8 and there is a lack of surgical fixation methods specifically targeted at longitudinal fractures of the patella.",
